&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;heading 2&quot;&gt;Looking for a role where Finance meets Supply Chain Operations?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134245418&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245529&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:261,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:261,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:300}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At&amp;nbsp;Infinitesima,&amp;nbsp;we&#39;re&amp;nbsp;building advanced metrology systems used by the world&#39;s leading semiconductor manufacturers to produce next-generation computer chips. Our technology helps enable the devices people&amp;nbsp;rely&amp;nbsp;on every day, from smartphones to AI infrastructure.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:300}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;As we continue to grow,&amp;nbsp;we&#39;re&amp;nbsp;looking for an&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Accounts &amp;amp; Supply Chain Administrator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; to join our team in Abingdon. This is more than a typical accounts support role.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role would suit someone who already has experience in a purchasing, supply chain, ERP administration, accounts payable or operations support environment and can quickly become productive with minimal supervision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll need to enjoy working independently, following established processes and taking ownership of a high-volume administrative workload. This is not a role where you&#39;ll be constantly directed day-to-day, so you&#39;ll need the confidence to manage priorities, solve routine problems and proactively chase colleagues for the information needed to keep orders, invoices and transactions moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Essential&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in a purchasing, supply chain, ERP administration, accounts payable or similar operational support role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Microsoft Excel and spreadsheet skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent numerical accuracy and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident working with large volumes of data entry and data validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable following established processes accurately and consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work independently and hit the ground running with minimal training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident communicating with colleagues at all levels of the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable persistently following up and chasing stakeholders for information, approvals and updates when required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, self-sufficient approach with a willingness to take ownership of tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Desirable&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using WinMan ERP, or a similar ERP/MRP system such as SAP, Oracle, Epicor, NetSuite or Microsoft Dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of purchasing processes, purchase orders, goods receipting and supplier management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience processing supplier invoices and reconciling transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience supporting both Supply Chain and Finance functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience maintaining accurate inventory, purchasing or operational records within an ERP system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;A Note About This Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re keen to be transparent about the nature of the position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for someone who enjoys structured work, maintaining accurate records, processing transactions, and ensuring data quality within business systems. &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A significant proportion of your time will be spent entering, checking and validating information within our ERP and finance systems.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role comes from being thorough, organised and persistent rather than constantly seeking new projects. &lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll enjoy this opportunity if you take pride in accuracy, process compliance and keeping the business running smoothly behind the scenes.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While you will gain exposure to both Finance and Supply Chain activities, this is not intended to be a fast-track management or leadership role, and progression opportunities are likely to be limited. We are therefore looking for someone who enjoys this type of operational work and is motivated by doing it well rather than viewing it as a stepping stone to another position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the accurate processing of supplier invoices and purchasing transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain data integrity within WinMan and other business systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, update and validate purchasing, inventory and supplier records&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow up with engineers, managers and other stakeholders to obtain missing information and approvals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve discrepancies between purchase orders, goods receipts and supplier invoices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce and maintain accurate records and audit trails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the smooth operation of the Supply Chain and Finance functions through accurate and timely administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help improve process efficiency and data quality as the business grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;heading 2&quot;&gt;Interested?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134245418&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245529&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:261,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:261,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:300}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;If&amp;nbsp;you&#39;re&amp;nbsp;organised, detail-focused and enjoy bringing order to complex processes,&amp;nbsp;we&#39;d&amp;nbsp;love to hear from you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:300}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A bit about us:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Infinitesima&amp;nbsp;is a privately owned company founded in 2001, as a spin-out of the University of Bristol, by CTO Professor Andrew Humphris. Our dynamic team of scientists and engineers is focussed on enabling the next generation of semiconductor devices through delivery of innovative products to customers around the world.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Your recruitment journey:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;1st stage:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;(45 minute) Remote meeting to evaluate your experience and technical ability&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;2nd stage:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;(2.5 hours) Face to face onsite evaluating technical,&amp;nbsp;presentation&amp;nbsp;and communication skills along with your ways of working and your opportunity to&amp;nbsp;gt&amp;nbsp;to know more about us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Our strength lies in the varied perspectives that come from&amp;nbsp;different cultures, experiences, and identities. We believe that true innovation is fuelled by collaboration, locally and globally. We strive to foster an environment where everyone can contribute meaningfully and thrive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;If you require adjustments to take part in the recruitment process, please let us know,&amp;nbsp;we’ll&amp;nbsp;do our best to support you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;If you prefer your camera off for a remote interview, just let us know, it&#39;s fine with us. We&#39;ll just say a quick hello first.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Note to recruitment agencies:&amp;nbsp;Infinitesima&amp;nbsp;Ltd only works with approved agencies and does not accept unsolicited agency CVs. Please do not&amp;nbsp;submit&amp;nbsp;candidate details in response to this advert, or to any&amp;nbsp;Infinitesima&amp;nbsp;Ltd employees.&amp;nbsp;Infinitesima&amp;nbsp;Ltd is not responsible for any fees related to unsolicited CVs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A note on how we run interviews:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We use AI only to transcribe our interviews so we can focus fully on you instead of scribbling notes. The AI does not take part in any decision making at any stage. All hiring decisions are made by real humans based on the conversation we have with you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Location and work pattern:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;All of&amp;nbsp;our new UK team members are asked to work on site here at Abingdon during their first three months with us. We offer flexible, hybrid working where possible upon completion of probation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This tends to be limited to Friday&#39;s due to the nature of the role which requires access to secure, onsite systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;This vacancy is not eligible for VISA sponsorship.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Castrol is one of the world’s leading lubricant brands, serving customers and consumers in the automotive, marine, industrial and energy sectors. Castrol brands are recognised globally for their premium quality and high performance, shaped by the company’s commitment to innovation and cutting-edge technology. With products sold in more than 150 countries, Castrol has helped keep things moving on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt; roads &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;and racetracks, air, sea, and space for over 125 years.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot; data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot;&gt;Whether you&#39;re just starting out or ready for your next big move, you&#39;re in the right place to explore an exciting career with Castrol.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(65, 145, 76);&quot; data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot;&gt;Job description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;About the Team&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Castrol, we don’t just make fluids, we help define the future of mobility, energy and digital infrastructure. The Advanced Electrification Testing (AET) team sits within Castrol’s Technology organisation and plays a critical role in supporting Research &amp;amp; Product Development by generating real-world performance data on lubricants, thermal management fluids and cooling technologies. Our mission is to understand how liquids perform inside the systems they are designed to protect and optimise, from electric vehicle batteries and ultra-fast chargers to high-performance data centres and advanced electronics.&lt;br&gt;As part of a major investment programme, Castrol’s Pangbourne Technology Centre is evolving into a centre of excellence for electrification and energy technologies. The team operates world-class testing facilities including battery cell, module and pack laboratories, high-voltage charging systems, immersion cooling tanks, data centre server environments and large-scale thermal management test rigs.&lt;br&gt;This is a team for engineers who are naturally curious. You&#39;ll work in an environment that combines the freedom of university-style research with the pace and impact of commercial product development. One day you may be investigating battery cooling performance, the next developing new testing methodologies for data centre technologies or semiconductor cooling systems.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll join a highly collaborative group of engineers, technicians, graduates and researchers who are passionate about solving complex engineering challenges. We are looking for individuals who love understanding how things work, enjoy getting hands-on with equipment, and want to help create the next generation of high-performance technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Key Tasks&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Engineer, you will lead research and development testing projects from concept through to final technical recommendations, working closely with internal stakeholders, technology experts and external partners.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Key responsibilities include:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Leading end-to-end testing and engineering projects supporting Castrol&#39;s research and product development programmes.&lt;br&gt;- Designing, building, commissioning and operating advanced test rigs and experimental systems.&lt;br&gt;- Developing innovative testing methodologies for emerging technologies across electric vehicles, batteries, charging infrastructure and data centres.&lt;br&gt;- Designing experiments using statistical Design of Experiments (DoE) techniques and ensuring data quality and repeatability.&lt;br&gt;- Performing advanced data analysis and translating results into meaningful engineering insights and recommendations.&lt;br&gt;- Working hands-on with high-voltage systems, instrumentation, thermal management equipment and power electronics.&lt;br&gt;- Supporting the installation, operation and continuous improvement of testing facilities and equipment.&lt;br&gt;- Acting as a subject matter expert in one or more areas such as battery systems, thermal management, data centres, cooling technologies, power electronics or DC power systems.&lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Collaborating with OEMs, technology partners and internal stakeholders to deliver co-engineered solutions.&lt;br&gt;- Coaching and mentoring engineers, technicians, graduates and interns while acting as a technical role model within the team.&lt;br&gt;- Identifying new technologies, testing opportunities and research directions that strengthen Castrol&#39;s innovation capability.&lt;br&gt;- Representing Castrol externally through technical engagement with customers, industry partners and research organisations.&lt;br&gt;- Maintaining the highest standards of safety, operational excellence and engineering integrity across all activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Experience Required&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced, hands-on engineer with a passion for experimentation, problem-solving and developing new technologies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will typically bring:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Degree-qualified in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Physics or a related engineering discipline.&lt;br&gt;- 5+ years&#39; experience in a professional engineering environment or equivalent in academia.&lt;br&gt;- A strong background in engineering testing, experimental design and data-driven problem solving.&lt;br&gt;- Experience designing, building or operating complex test equipment and test rigs.&lt;br&gt;- Exposure to safety-critical or operational engineering environments.&lt;br&gt;- Knowledge of high-voltage electrical systems (typically &amp;gt;60V DC) and safe working practices.&lt;br&gt;- Strong technical reporting, communication and stakeholder management skills.&lt;br&gt;- The ability to work autonomously while leading projects and influencing technical direction.&lt;br&gt;- A curiosity-driven mindset and a genuine passion for engineering and technology.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Expertise in at least one of the following areas:&lt;br&gt;- Electric vehicle propulsion systems&lt;br&gt;- Battery technologies&lt;br&gt;- Thermal management and cooling systems&lt;br&gt;- Data centre technologies&lt;br&gt;- DC power systems&lt;br&gt;- Power electronics&lt;br&gt;- Electronics and instrumentation&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Desirable experience includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Master&#39;s degree, PhD or progression towards Chartered Engineer status.&lt;br&gt;- Experience of battery thermal management, immersion cooling or liquid cooling technologies.&lt;br&gt;- Knowledge of semiconductor or chip cooling applications.&lt;br&gt;- Experience with advanced measurement techniques, data analytics or CAE tools.&lt;br&gt;- Published technical papers or involvement in research programmes.&lt;br&gt;- Experience gained within automotive, battery, aerospace, power, data centre or advanced research environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for engineers who want more than a traditional testing position. If you&#39;re excited by the opportunity to innovate, develop new ideas, work across batteries, data centres, charging systems and emerging technologies, and have access to world-class facilities to turn concepts into reality, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(65, 145, 76);&quot;&gt;Privacy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot;&gt;The Castrol entity recruiting for this role is the data controller for the personal information you provide. We use it to assess your application and to manage the recruitment and onboarding process. We may share it with service providers who support our recruitment, and it may be transferred to other Castrol entities internationally under appropriate safeguards. We keep it only for as long as necessary. For details of how we use your information and your data protection rights, contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a id=&quot;OWAcac3778b-aec2-4e71-7765-87f7daa1b8b6&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot; ----- -----
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, gender, gender expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, socioeconomic status, neurodiversity/neurocognitive functioning, veteran status or disability status. Individuals with an accessibility need may request an adjustment/accommodation related to Castrol recruiting process (e.g., accessing the job application, completing required assessments, participating in telephone screenings or interviews, etc.).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you are selected for a position and depending upon your role, your employment may be contingent upon adherence to local policy. This may include pre-placement drug screening, medical review of physical fitness for the role, and background checks.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Castrol is one of the world’s leading lubricant brands, serving customers and consumers in the automotive, marine, industrial and energy sectors. Castrol brands are recognised globally for their premium quality and high performance, shaped by the company’s commitment to innovation and cutting-edge technology. With products sold in more than 150 countries, Castrol has helped keep things moving on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt; roads &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;and racetracks, air, sea, and space for over 125 years.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot; data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot;&gt;Whether you&#39;re just starting out or ready for your next big move, you&#39;re in the right place to explore an exciting career with Castrol.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(65, 145, 76);&quot; data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot;&gt;Job description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;About the team&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join Castrol&#39;s Global Pricing team, reporting to the Global Strategic Pricing Manager and leading a small team of data scientists and analysts. Working alongside colleagues with pricing and commercial expertise, you&#39;ll combine technical problem-solving with developing others, turning your team&#39;s analysis into decisions that improve revenue, margin and product mix.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Key tasks&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Which pricing questions are worth solving, and how do you turn the answers into something the business can use? You&#39;ll help connect the commercial problem, the analytical approach and the practical solution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find where margin is being lost across discounts, rebates and trade investments. Quantify the opportunity, recommend corrective action and support governance of pricing corridors, floors and exceptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the business make better product-price-pack and portfolio choices across DIY, DIFM and B2B channels. Explore customers, segments, specifications, pack sizes and tiers to inform price positioning and the price steps between offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deploy models for elasticity, demand forecasting, willingness to pay, price sensitivity, scenarios and price optimisation, translating the results into recommendations people can act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn recurring work into repeatable tools. Design automation for price changes, analysis, reporting and decision support, reducing manual intervention and making solutions usable across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop your analytical team, encouraging commercial curiosity and innovation. Set priorities around business value, plan projects and help colleagues turn their technical work into practical outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Pricing, Sales, Finance and Marketing, using clear explanations of the evidence to influence senior stakeholders and connect analytical findings to commercial decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success means more than delivering a model: it means measurable commercial impact, pricing processes that need less manual effort, and a team that understands its priorities and develops its capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Experience required&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t need a long management career behind you. You&#39;ll need technical depth, evidence that your analysis makes a difference, and the aptitude to help others do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A university degree or higher, with proven experience in pricing analytics, data science or operations research, ideally in a commercial environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong mathematical and statistical modelling skills, including regression, machine learning and segmentation, and the ability to apply them to questions such as demand forecasting, elasticity and price optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in analytical tools such as Python, R and SQL and visualisation platforms such as Power BI or Tableau, with experience working with large datasets and building scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of translating analysis into business impact, supported by commercial judgement, problem-solving and decision-making skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability and aptitude to lead and develop a small analytical team. Previous leadership or mentoring experience is valuable, but strong technical candidates with less management experience will also be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering and leading projects, with the initiative, planning, prioritisation and collaborative approach needed to keep work moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent written and spoken English, with the ability to explain complex findings, influence stakeholders at different levels and build relationships within and beyond Global Pricing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desirable: pricing or revenue growth management experience, including gross-to-net, trade spend and portfolio/mix optimisation. Strong transferable data science or operations research experience is welcome, with scope to learn the pricing domain; exposure to automation tools and workflows is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(65, 145, 76);&quot;&gt;Privacy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot;&gt;The Castrol entity recruiting for this role is the data controller for the personal information you provide. We use it to assess your application and to manage the recruitment and onboarding process. We may share it with service providers who support our recruitment, and it may be transferred to other Castrol entities internationally under appropriate safeguards. We keep it only for as long as necessary. For details of how we use your information and your data protection rights, contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a id=&quot;OWAcac3778b-aec2-4e71-7765-87f7daa1b8b6&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot; ----- -----
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, gender, gender expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, socioeconomic status, neurodiversity/neurocognitive functioning, veteran status or disability status. Individuals with an accessibility need may request an adjustment/accommodation related to Castrol recruiting process (e.g., accessing the job application, completing required assessments, participating in telephone screenings or interviews, etc.).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you are selected for a position and depending upon your role, your employment may be contingent upon adherence to local policy. This may include pre-placement drug screening, medical review of physical fitness for the role, and background checks.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Castrol is one of the world’s leading lubricant brands, serving customers and consumers in the automotive, marine, industrial and energy sectors. Castrol brands are recognised globally for their premium quality and high performance, shaped by the company’s commitment to innovation and cutting-edge technology. With products sold in more than 150 countries, Castrol has helped keep things moving on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt; roads &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;and racetracks, air, sea, and space for over 125 years.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot; data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot;&gt;Whether you&#39;re just starting out or ready for your next big move, you&#39;re in the right place to explore an exciting career with Castrol.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(65, 145, 76);&quot; data-ogsc=&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot;&gt;Job description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;About the team&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Castrol Technology develops the products, technologies and technical solutions that power Castrol’s performance today while creating opportunities for future growth. Bringing together global expertise across seven Technology Centres in formulation science, chemistry, engineering, product development and testing, we co-engineer solutions that optimise performance for customers across traditional lubricant applications and emerging technologies.&lt;br&gt;We’re now hiring a Lubricants Senior Technologist to join our UK Technology Centre in Reading, supporting the Castrol Europe Performance Unit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be part of the Technology Deployment Team, working at the interface between Global R&amp;amp;D, Sales, Marketing, Supply Chain, manufacturing and OEM technology teams. The team plays a critical role in turning product innovation into commercially successful solutions for customers across Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly collaborative role for someone who combines strong technical expertise with commercial awareness and stakeholder influence. You’ll have the opportunity to work across functions and markets, shape the successful introduction of new lubricant technologies and help solve complex technical challenges for one of the world’s most recognised lubricant brands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Key tasks&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the deployment of new lubricant formulations and products across European markets, coordinating activity across technology, sales, marketing, supply chain and manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer and market requirements into clear technical requirements for product development teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Embed Quality Assurance processes across the plants and conduct Quality Assurance assessments with 3&lt;em&gt;rd&lt;/em&gt; parties&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a key technical interface between product development, OEM technology, marketing, sales, supply chain and customer-facing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate technical specifications, blending requirements, plant trials, testing and formulation approvals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical troubleshooting support for manufacturing and blending issues, including raw material shortages, quality incidents and customer complaints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure product claims are technically substantiated and aligned with regulatory and marketing requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver technical communications and training to support new product launches, adapting global materials for regional and local audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical input into tenders, new market opportunities, procurement evaluations and formulation optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve formulation cost competitiveness, supply resilience and overall product performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Experience Required&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in chemistry, engineering or a closely related technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical knowledge of lubricants, lubricant formulations and automotive applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical formulation experience within lubricants or fuels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of engine mechanics and the performance requirements placed on lubricants and fuels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of automotive industry trends and their implications for lubricant technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking ownership of formulation or technical programmes from development through to deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional stakeholder management skills, with the ability to build effective networks across technical and commercial teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence presenting technical information externally, advocating for products and communicating with larger audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial awareness, including formulation optimisation, cost competitiveness and supply resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly learn and apply new technical knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of how technology, sales, marketing, supply chain and product development work together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal and presentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using digital collaboration tools and basic modelling or analytical tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(65, 145, 76);&quot;&gt;Privacy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot;&gt;The Castrol entity recruiting for this role is the data controller for the personal information you provide. We use it to assess your application and to manage the recruitment and onboarding process. We may share it with service providers who support our recruitment, and it may be transferred to other Castrol entities internationally under appropriate safeguards. We keep it only for as long as necessary. For details of how we use your information and your data protection rights, contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a id=&quot;OWAcac3778b-aec2-4e71-7765-87f7daa1b8b6&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot; ----- -----
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, gender, gender expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, socioeconomic status, neurodiversity/neurocognitive functioning, veteran status or disability status. Individuals with an accessibility need may request an adjustment/accommodation related to Castrol recruiting process (e.g., accessing the job application, completing required assessments, participating in telephone screenings or interviews, etc.).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(101, 101, 101);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you are selected for a position and depending upon your role, your employment may be contingent upon adherence to local policy. This may include pre-placement drug screening, medical review of physical fitness for the role, and background checks.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BVNK is the stablecoin-powered financial stack for enterprises. We&#39;re now part of Mastercard, and together we&#39;re building a network for every form of money – one that delivers more reach, more capability and more choice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We enable businesses to build financial products, unlock new markets, and move money in seconds across 130+ countries, with 40+ licenses for fiat and digital assets globally. Processing billions annually, we empower enterprises worldwide to send, receive, convert, and settle stablecoins and fiat seamlessly through a single integration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our mission is to accelerate global money movement, and we&#39;re assembling a world-class team to make it happen.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trusted by industry leaders like Corpay, Worldpay, Deel, and Flywire, we deliver the infrastructure that makes new forms of money usable within the financial systems customers already rely on today.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By combining Mastercard&#39;s global payment reach and trusted networks with BVNK&#39;s stablecoin infrastructure, we&#39;re building the trusted operating layer for the evolution of money movement, helping customers participate in emerging digital networks without having to rebuild their businesses around every new innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a diverse team spread across EMEA, North America, and APAC, with a shared belief that stablecoins are the new infrastructure layer for financial services, and that BVNK is at the forefront of this shift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re incredibly honored to have been recognized by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CNBC World&#39;s Top Fintech Companies (2026)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FXC Intelligence Top 100 Cross-border Payment Companies (2026)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Newsweek&#39;s The Top 100 Global Most Loved Workplaces (three years running, most recently 2025)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LinkedIn as one of the Top 20 Startups in the UK (2025)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this role in the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Product Manager to own the product vision, strategy, and delivery for the Reporting &amp;amp; Customer Reconciliation subdomain within BVNK&#39;s Ledger domain. You&#39;ll&amp;nbsp; work closely with engineering, design, finance, operations, and commercial teams to define how BVNK&#39;s customers&amp;nbsp; and BVNK&#39;s own internal teams — see, understand, and trust their financial data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Ledger domain is the financial backbone of BVNK, a single, trusted source of truth for all customer and transactional balances across products, currencies, and rails. Within this domain, the Reporting &amp;amp; Customer Reconciliation subdomain is responsible for providing clear, consistent financial views derived from the ledger for both internal and external reporting. Through the Reporting Service, Search Service, and downstream data surfaces,it ensures that positions, balances, and movements are accurately represented for Finance, Risk, Operations, and customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact, cross-functional role. As part of BVNK&#39;s Billing 2.0 vision and the drive toward a 100% self-serve customer experience, you&#39;ll define and deliver the product capabilities that give customers full transparency; enabling them to reconcile invoices, audit charges programmatically, and automate close processes, while also building the internal reporting foundations that Finance, Reconciliation, and Operations depend on to scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Areas of Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the product vision and roadmap for Reporting &amp;amp; Customer Reconciliation&lt;/strong&gt; — Define the strategy for how BVNK exposes financial data to customers and internal teams, aligning with the broader Ledger domain mission and company objectives (Billing 2.0, self-serve experience, MiCA compliance).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive transaction report fee breakdowns&lt;/strong&gt; — Define requirements and work with engineering to ensure transaction reports and APIs properly include both real-time and invoiced fees, broken down by fee type&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the customer reconciliation product &lt;/strong&gt;— Define and deliver customer-facing reconciliation endpoints and reporting surfaces that enable enterprise clients to programmatically audit charges, automate close processes, and reconcile against invoices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve internal financial reporting&lt;/strong&gt; — Partner with Finance, Reconciliation, and Operations to understand their data needs and deliver standardised reports and views that replace fragmented, manual processes with reliable, automated data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate across domains &lt;/strong&gt;— Work with the Billing &amp;amp; Fees, Wallets, Balances , Digital Assets, Treasury, and Reconciliation domain to ensure reporting data is consistent and accurate end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define reporting for multi-entity and regulatory requirements&lt;/strong&gt; — As BVNK expands across jurisdictions and customer types, ensure reporting structures correctly represent entity-specific data, segregation requirements, and regulatory obligations (MiCA safekeeping, EMI reconciliation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own stakeholder relationships &lt;/strong&gt;— Serve as the primary product contact for Reporting &amp;amp; Customer Reconciliation. Engage regularly with Commercial (AMs/CSMs), Finance, Operations, and enterprise customers to gather requirements, validate solutions, and communicate roadmap priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure and iterate&lt;/strong&gt; — Define and track KPIs for reporting accuracy, customer adoption of reconciliation tools, reduction in manual reconciliation effort, and internal stakeholder satisfaction. Use data to inform roadmap prioritisation and demonstrate impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ship with quality&lt;/strong&gt; — Write clear PRDs, user stories, and acceptance criteria. Participate in architecture reviews and technical design submissions. Run beta programmes with select customers and internal teams to validate reporting capabilities before general availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we need from you:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience in fintech, payments, or financial services — ideally with exposure to ledger systems, financial reporting, or reconciliation products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of financial data and reporting — you&#39;ve worked with transaction data, balance reporting, reconciliation workflows, or invoicing systems. You understand concepts like double-entry bookkeeping, ledger postings, balance snapshots, and fee structures or can learn them quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building internal and customer-facing data products — you&#39;ve defined and delivered reporting APIs, dashboards, data exports, or reconciliation tools that serve both external customers and internal operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills — you&#39;re comfortable working with engineering, finance, operations, compliance, and commercial teams. You can translate complex financial requirements into clear product specifications and negotiate priorities across stakeholders with competing needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven decision making — you use quantitative and qualitative data to inform roadmap decisions, measure product impact, and communicate outcomes to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency — you don&#39;t need to write code, but you can engage meaningfully with engineers on API design, data models, event-driven architectures, and database schemas. You&#39;re comfortable with tools like Snowflake, QuickSight, or similar BI/data warehousing platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a fast-paced, scaling environment — you&#39;ve operated in a startup or scale-up where scope is broad, resources are constrained, and you need to make pragmatic trade-offs between ideal and achievable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication — you write clear PRDs, run effective stakeholder meetings, and can present product strategy to senior leadership with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-first mindset — you&#39;re effectively working across time zones in an asynchronous-first culture, using Slack, Confluence, and Jira as primary collaboration tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with regulated financial services (EMI, VASP) and compliance reporting requirements (MiCA, safeguarding, client money rules).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in B2B payments platforms, stablecoin infrastructure, or crypto-adjacent products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with reconciliation platforms (Duco, Xero, or similar) and financial ledger systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with multi-tenant architectures and entity-level data segregation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of event-driven data pipelines (Kafka, outbox patterns) and how they impact data consistency in reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product experience with self-serve billing or invoicing platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you can expect from us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fair and &lt;strong&gt;competitive salary&lt;/strong&gt; at every stage of your growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible working&lt;/strong&gt; hours, with hybrid working at its heart&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;culture&lt;/strong&gt; built on passionate, growth-minded people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;flexible approach to holiday&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to travel to our &lt;strong&gt;offices around the world&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An &lt;strong&gt;open and creative environment&lt;/strong&gt; where you can help us define the future of BVNK, its culture, and its opportunity sets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At BVNK, we are focused on building a diverse and inclusive team. While you may not meet all of our requirements, we’d encourage you to apply if you meet the majority of our expectations. You may be a great fit for this role or another role in our team. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation packages are based on candidate experience and relevant certifications.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Bulgaria Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€90.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€115.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation packages are based on candidate experience and relevant certifications.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Spain Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€90.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€115.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation packages are based on candidate experience and relevant certifications.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Malta Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€90.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€115.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation packages are based on candidate experience and relevant certifications.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Poland Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€90.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€115.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated Test Manager to lead Quality Assurance for a AAA game development team. You will lead embedded testing teams, and partner with cross-functional leadership to balance quality, schedule, and risk in a complex development environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we will do together:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;QA Strategy &amp;amp; Leadership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define global QA strategy, test objectives, quality gates, and risk-based testing methodologies for major project milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate QA into early development planning to ensure quality is a core part of the feature lifecycle rather than just final validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;People Management&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop a high-performing team of QA Leads and testers, fostering a culture of ownership and collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage both internal and external QA resources effectively to meet project demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Test Planning &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee comprehensive test execution across functional, gameplay, performance, stability, multiplayer, and platform certification areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor defect trends and quality risks, ensuring critical issues are prioritized and driven to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Defect &amp;amp; Risk Management&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze defect data to identify systemic quality issues and drive root-cause analysis and preventative initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate emerging quality risks and technical assessments clearly to Production and project leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Milestone &amp;amp; Release Management&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish QA schedules and deliverables for major milestones, providing objective assessments of build stability and release readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate final regression and stabilization efforts during high-pressure release periods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Platform Certification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead preparation for first-party certification, coordinating test plans and tracking submission risks to ensure successful launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for quality as the senior QA representative within project leadership, balancing technical standards with production constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong partnerships across disciplines to establish a shared responsibility for quality across the entire development team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;External &amp;amp; Co-Development QA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage external vendors and co-development QA teams, defining expectations and reporting standards to ensure seamless integration with internal strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;QA Tools, Metrics &amp;amp; Process Improvement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement data-driven reporting and dashboards to track build health, test coverage, and milestone progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve QA efficiency through automation, tooling, and process retrospectives.&lt;/li&gt;
