&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;In a nutshell, &lt;strong&gt;your key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt; will consist in:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and grow a portfolio of strategic partners: build, develop, and nurture long‑term, high‑impact relationships; lead initiatives that create new opportunities and drive revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set strategy and expand scope: manage expansion (new geographies, new use cases/features), optimize existing programs, and define the roadmap for joint projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross‑functional leadership and negotiation: align Product, Sales, Marketing, Legal, Finance, Regulatory, etc. to shape value‑add operating models; build business cases and negotiate/close contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End‑to‑end execution: drive partnership initiatives from idea to validation, launch, and scale; coordinate internal and external stakeholders throughout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance management: define KPIs/OKRs, monitor results, surface insights, and implement improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner enablement and activation: ensure partners are equipped to market, sell, and support Alma; create playbooks and internal enablement materials; share best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Joint go‑to‑market and growth: design and run partner‑led and partner‑assisted GTM plans, including co‑marketing and co‑selling programs that accelerate commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Representation and relationship stewardship: be the single point of contact (SPOC); represent Alma to the partner and the partner within Alma; cultivate a dynamic partner community and long‑term, trusted relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity development: proactively identify, validate, and secure new opportunities with existing partners.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
